<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shimazu clan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Shimazu were a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a> clan of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a> who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satsuma-domain">Satsuma</a> from the late 12th century to 1871, one of the longest unbroken lordships in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. In the 1580s they nearly conquered all of Kyushu before submitting to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> in 1587. Under the Tokugawa they held the Satsuma Domain, subjugated the Ryukyu Kingdom in 1609, and helped lead the overthrow of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a> in 1868.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shimazu-clan.jpg" alt="Shimazu clan" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sarang · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maru_ni_J%C5%AB-monji_(Kutsuwa)_inverted.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
